Summary
Action Against Hunger is currently looking to fill the role of Mental Health, Psychosocial Support, and Protection (MHPSS) Officer, who will be responsible to provide high-quality psychological assessments, interventions, and care to vulnerable populations, including children, adolescents, adults, and families.
The role involves conducting individual and group therapeutic sessions, training and supervising non-specialists, ensuring confidentiality and proper documentation, and collaborating with other departments and stakeholders.
