Job Description:
Job Description
The Vice-Chancellor is the Chief Executive, Chief Accounting and Academic Head of the University, ex-officio member of the Governing Council, Chairman of Senate and Chairman of Congregation. The Vice-Chancellor is the Chief Exponent of all the educational missions of the University and his/her office serves as the nerve centre of all activities including protocol, extremal relations and the coordination of various internal organs of the University.
The Vice-Chancellor exercises general superintendence over the University and regulates the admission of students, subject to the guidelines and procedures approved by the University Senate and other relevant statutory agencies. The Vice-Chancellor sees to the day-to-day administration and ensures that the provisions of the Laws, Statutes, Ordinances and Regulations of the University are observed.
The Vice-Chancellor shall;
at all times advise the Governing Council on any matters affecting the finance, and the administration of the University;
ibe responsible to the Governing Council in maintaining peace, order and efficient management of the affairs and ensuring the enforcement of the Laws, Statutes, Ordinances and Regulations of the University and
be responsible to the Governing Council for discipline in the University.
The Candidate
The Candidate for this post must be a distinguished scholar with outstanding academic and administrative records and proven manager of human, financial and material resources. Interested Candidates must therefore, meet and provide verifiable evidence of the following underlisted qualities and qualifications
Possess a Doctorate Degree from a recognised University, except for Professors of Medicine;
be a University teacher of the rank of Professor, attained for at least ten (10) years in a highly regarded and reputable institution, as at the time of applying for the position;
be a person of high academic standing and reputation in his or her respective discipline and conversant with the developmental academic and other complex managerial challenges of a fast-growing University;
possess a proven and demonstrable ability to attract international research and Development grants;
possess clear vision for further growth and advancement of the University and realization of its vision, mission and strategic goals;
must be morally sound and of unimpeachable probity and integrity;
must be mentally and physically fit in a state of good heath;
and should not be more than sixty-five (65) years old as at the date of possible assumption of office in February, 2026.
Terms and Conditions of Service Applicable to the Position
The successful applicant shall hold the position for a single term of five (5) years on such conditions as may be specified in the letter of appointment. The recommendation and other condition of service are as applicable to the position of the Vice-Chancellor in all Federal Universities in Nigeria and as may be determined from time to time by the Federal Government of Nigeria/Governing Council of the University.

PURPOSE
The holder of this position would provide supervision and promotes and values participatory approaches throughout the project cycle (identification of beneficiaries, awareness raising and sensitisation, committee formation, preparing and delivering messages, food distribution Pre and Post Distribution Monitoring (PDM) as well as monitoring and evaluation under direct supervision of FSL Field Coordinator. During absence of Field Coordinator, position will be wholly accountable for given activities under direct supervision of Deputy Project Manager.
RESPONSIBILITIES
Specifically:
Facilitate INTERSOS staff, donors’ program staff visiting in field and other key stakeholders for a coordinated implementation of project activities
Line management for the casual worker / enumerator working for specific activities
Coordinate, supervise and manage CBT and food distribution activities within project implementation as per plan and report same;
Participate and provide primary level information / Assessment / Analysis in a timely & accurately manner;
Provide regular progress reports to the FSL Field Coordinator;
Understand, implement and / or maintain standard INTERSOS inventory management policies and procedures.
Participate in monitoring, PDMs / assessment / verification process
Implement other tasks as might be required with relation to the INTERSOS Country Program in Nigeria.
POSITION REQUIREMENTS
Qualifications and Experience
University Bachelor's degree or Higher National Diploma;
Minimum 3 years of experience from at national level project implementation position in a humanitarian / recovery context;
Experience in working in complex and volatile contexts;
Technical Food Security expertise (ware house management, In-kind and cash for food);
Documented results related to the position’s responsibilities;
Experience in leadership and problem solving;
Fluency in English, both written and oral including local language will be advantage;
Capacity to adapt to basic living conditions, patience;
Ability to put up with pressure from government agencies;
Ability to deliver high quality work within tight deadlines;
Strong negotiation skills;

Description and Objectives
The Human Resource Intern will support the Talent team and all staff and perform a variety of tasks.
The primary duty of the human resource intern is to support the Talent team in the well-functioning of the day-to-day management of HR-related needs and develop subsequent plans and solutions that align HR management with SCIDaR objectives.
He/She is responsible for providing support in the administration of HR functions, among others. Additionally, you will be required to perform other tasks as may be assigned.
Core Requirements
Compelling evidence of interest in and commitment to the mission of SCIDaR;
Ability to handle sensitive situations and maintain a high degree of confidentiality;
Demonstrated good strategic thinking, problem-solving, and thought leadership abilities;
Advanced computer usage skills with proficiency in Microsoft® Word, Excel, PowerPoint;
Fast learner, open to learning from peers, subordinates and supervisors collaboratively and at a rapid pace;
Results-oriented performer, experienced in developing and tracking self and team with clear KPIs;
Strong verbal and written communication skills.
Education and Experience:
Minimum of a first-class in degree in Human resources management, Social Sciences, or related discipline;
Familiarity with filing and archiving, training, recruitment, event planning, and other HR functions;
Excellent analytical, administrative, and organizational skills for meticulous task management;
Proficiency with MS office tools, Google workspace, and digital applications/platforms;
Knowledge of data analysis tools llike Power BI is an added advantage;
Demonstrated interest in building a career in human resources.
